& [ObservedBoundary] distinguishes invocation from cycle
  + exact CycleReport replay begins only after command arguments field provider endpoint and model identity have been admitted
  + model discovery currently performs provider I O before CycleReport construction
  + a discovery transport fault therefore has honest stderr and nonzero exit but no replayable machine account
  + contract and verify ignore trailing arguments while run and control overwrite duplicate recognized option values
  + evidence publication itself can fail and no design can truthfully claim a file contains its own failed write

& [Delineation] separates three identities
  + Invocation is the caller-supplied command operation arguments and intended evidence destinations
  + Cycle is FIELD_ATTEND DELINEATE LATCH after exact invocation field endpoint and model admission
  + Publication is the attempt to make an already formed account or report durable
  + a failure in one identity must not be relabeled as failure or success in another
  - never: represent failure to publish an account as a successfully persisted account

& [RecommendedFlow] stages observable work before inference
  + PARSE_EXACT then ACCOUNT_INVOCATION then VALIDATE_FIELD then ADMIT_PROVIDER then RESOLVE_MODEL then BEGIN_CYCLE then VERIFY_REPORT then PUBLISH_CREATE_NEW then EMIT_OUTCOME
  + exact parsing rejects unknown trailing duplicate missing and ambiguous arguments before file reads provider calls directory creation or output writes
  + governed run and control require explicit model identity
  + optional model discovery becomes a separate DISCOVER_MODEL operation with its own typed outcome and no implied cycle start
  + every stage carries one exact predecessor digest and cannot skip forward

& [ProposedMachineForm] is FieldCycleInvocationOutcome
  + profile job_id operation and canonical length-prefixed argv_digest bind supplied invocation identity
  + command_status is admitted refused or faulted
  + reached_stage is parse_exact field_validated provider_admitted model_resolved cycle_reported or publication_attempted
  + field_digest provider_base_url and model are present only after their corresponding stage succeeds
  + cycle_report_sha256 and cycle_terminal_state are present only after independent CycleReport verification
  + publication_status is not_attempted published or failed
  + published_path and published_file_sha256 exist only for published
  + fault_code fault_stage sanitized_detail and detail_sha256 keep refusal inspectable without arbitrary secret retention
  + predecessor_digest outcome_digest and closed event ordinals bind the account
  + no field makes preflight admission semantic truth effect authority or production trust

& [ProposedDiscoveryForm] is ModelDiscoveryOutcome
  + exact canonical loopback endpoint request profile response byte ceiling proxy denial redirect denial and time ceilings are explicit
  + discovered model IDs remain provider observations and do not become signed SOP identities
  + non-success status body length and body digest are retained without arbitrary response body text
  + a successful discovery outcome may supply explicit model input to a later separately digested invocation
  + discovery never starts FIELD_ATTEND or creates a CycleReport

& [PublicationBoundary] is machine-clean but not magical
  + stdout emits one typed InvocationOutcome whenever the process can serialize one
  + governed live invocation should require a create-new account destination distinct from the CycleReport destination
  + account publication precedes provider I O only if the format supports an immutable admitted-intent record and successor outcome linkage
  + final outcome publication uses no-overwrite semantics and records the admitted-intent predecessor
  + OS failure before stdout serialization or during all evidence-channel writes remains an exterior process fault and must not be claimed persisted
  + crash atomicity durability and multi-consumer commit remain separate platform requirements

& [Compatibility] preserves the P0 corpus
  + CycleReport profile request profiles report bytes canonical replay hashes and h8 remain unchanged
  + InvocationOutcome and ModelDiscoveryOutcome use new profiles and verifiers rather than reinterpreting historical reports
  + existing valid exact run control verify fixture contract and field-digest invocations retain their successful meanings
  + formerly ignored trailing or duplicate inputs become deterministic refusals before effects
  + a successor executable receives a new deployment identity and never replaces h8 evidence retroactively

& [HeldOutAcceptanceSketch] is falsifiable
  + [FEP1-001] every command rejects one trailing token and every duplicate option before file network or write effects
  + [FEP1-002] missing value unknown option option permutation and exact valid invocation have deterministic outcomes
  + [FEP1-003] unreachable model discovery yields a replayable discovery fault with zero cycle and inference calls
  + [FEP1-004] explicit-model run reaches CycleReport construction without calling model discovery
  + [FEP1-005] invalid field missing field endpoint refusal and output collision remain distinct stages and codes
  + [FEP1-006] changed argv order field digest provider model stage event predecessor report digest or publication claim fails verification
  + [FEP1-007] a report write failure cannot carry published and an account write failure is visible on stdout without false durability
  + [FEP1-008] all thirty-two retained P0 reports replay byte-identically and all thirty-one provider reports retain their assurance distribution
  + [FEP1-009] local positive negative and control paths pass before optional EVO-X2 observation

& [DependencyOrder] is source then authority then pure parser
  + preserve user decision on invocation account persistence explicit-model policy discovery separation and exterior publication-fault semantics
  + run SJS over new forms error taxonomy event grammar effect order resource ceilings compatibility and authority
  + implement strict pure argument parser and outcome verifier before any provider adapter change
  + add discovery operation before altering run or control behavior
  + deploy only after retained-corpus replay and negative no-effect tests pass

& [RecommendedDecision] is separate discovery and explicit governed model
  + this removes provider I O from cycle preflight and gives discovery its own honest evidence identity
  + a separate InvocationOutcome closes command-level trace without weakening or overloading CycleReport
  + strict argument rejection can share the slice while remaining independently testable
  + publication failure must stay exterior to any file it prevented from existing
  + no implementation schema or compatibility policy is authorized by this recommendation alone
